    "For open and held topics, a named falsifier exists only when a note or reason contains a listed discriminating-observation phrase or a sentence with both a missing-measurement cue and one of the six named family vocabularies. A generic sentence such as 'more work is needed' does not qualify. Open without either is counted as unfalsifiable and never reported as well-posed.",
